    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the **salutation** feature: an owner may be created with an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and reads back a derived `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges, following the existing derived-field pattern in this codebase:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, and a derived `getSalutation()` that returns `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, otherwise just the last name.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` as an optional input property on the `OwnerFields` schema, and `salutation` as a `readOnly` derived property on the `Owner` schema. (DTOs are generated from this spec at build time; MapStruct auto-maps `title` and `salutation` by name.)\n\n3. **Database schemas** \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table in all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres), and appended the corresponding value to the positional owner inserts in `db/hsqldb/data.sql` (the file the tests load).\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors), confirming `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `salutation` = `\"DR who\"` for an owner created with title `DR` and last name `who`.",
